1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,249
Opportunity should have starved within months.

2
00:00:02,639 --> 00:00:05,050
Instead, again and again, Martian wind

3
00:00:05,060 --> 00:00:07,430
and passing dust devils swept its

4
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:08,330
panels clean.

5
00:00:09,060 --> 00:00:10,970
The team called them cleaning events.

6
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:12,810
Each one gave the rover back

7
00:00:12,820 --> 00:00:14,690
its power, and it kept driving.

8
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:17,050
Ninety days became years.

9
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:19,430
Years became more than fourteen.

10
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:22,710
Then, in 2018, a storm grew

11
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:24,370
until it wrapped the whole planet.

12
00:00:24,860 --> 00:00:26,890
The sky over Opportunity grew so

13
00:00:26,980 --> 00:00:29,450
dark that almost no sunlight reached

14
00:00:29,460 --> 00:00:30,210
its panels.

15
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:33,110
On the 10th of June, 2018,

16
00:00:33,440 --> 00:00:35,450
Opportunity sent its last signal.

17
00:00:36,260 --> 00:00:37,810
Engineers on Earth sent more than

18
00:00:37,820 --> 00:00:39,550
a thousand commands over the next

19
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:41,450
eight months asking it to wake

20
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:41,790
up.

21
00:00:42,440 --> 00:00:43,430
It never answered.

22
00:00:44,620 --> 00:00:46,610
What finally stopped the most successful

23
00:00:46,660 --> 00:00:48,370
rover of its time was not

24
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:49,670
cold or rock.

25
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:52,120
It was the sky turning off.
